[node name="tutorialtxt" type="Label" parent="gui/controlstutorialui/controlspanel/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(520, 0)
layout_mode = 2
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 27
text = "There are 4 different modes used in the editor. 
The select mode is used to modify properties and groups, and allow for objects to be moved.
The drag/move mode is used to move objects around.
The add mode is used to place new objects into the editor.
The delete mode is used to remove objects from the editor.
The menu button (3 lines) contains navigational buttons and other information and settings.
Playtesting your level just gives you one life to try out whatever you've added.
The properties window has all the properties for modifying an object like color, size, and more. Some objects (usually triggers) have additional custom properties.
The groups window is important for \"communication\" between objects. The group(s) an object has is an identifier. The targets an object has are what find the identifier and hook up the group to itself. Any object can have groups but only some objects can have targets (mostly triggers). The global groups manager can help edit big groups of objects.
The blocks category currently contains 2 types, regular blocks and d-blocks. Regular blocks still destroy the player. D-blocks (aka Sliding Blocks) enable sliding on the area that they cover.
Hazards are objects that destroy the player upon touching them.
Portals do a multitude of things that can vary gameplay like different gamemodes, different player sizes, teleportation, and such.
Interactables include pads and orbs. Pads trigger an effect when the player touches them, while orbs must be timed and the user must click when the player is touching the orb to trigger the effect.
Decorations are purely visual objects, as the name implies.
Triggers enable the changing of properties among other things. They are triggered whenever the player passes their position (doesn't have to be touched by the player). 
"
horizontal_alignment = 1
vertical_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 3

